---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import OrbStage from '../../components/OrbStage.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Lab · Tactile · Niyora"
  description="Experimental tactile layout preview. Not production."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.niyora.com/lab/home-tactile"
>
  <OrbStage />

  <div class="lab-label" aria-hidden="true">Lab: Tactile</div>

  <main class="tc">
    <section class="tc-hero" data-hue="335" data-sat="58%" data-orb-alpha="0.9" data-orb-scale="0.9">
      <div class="glass hero-card">
        <p class="brand">Niyora</p>
        <h1>Life doesn't wait for PMS. But we do.</h1>
        <p class="subhead">Niyora is a PMS app that sees your week coming. When feelings run high, it helps you reflect, regulate, and respond, instead of react.</p>
        <button type="button" class="btn">I'm interested</button>
        <p class="trust">Free · No account · No wearables · No cycle data shared</p>
        <p class="trust strong">Your personal details never reach the AI.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="330" data-sat="55%">
      <div class="glass slab center">
        <p class="eyebrow">Built on one fact</p>
        <h2>Women with emotional regulation skills handle PMS better.</h2>
        <p class="lead">That's the whole idea. Staying steady is a skill, not something you're born with, and skills can be learned. Niyora teaches it a little at a time, so the week gets easier to carry.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="300" data-sat="55%">
      <div class="head center">
        <p class="eyebrow">What no one told you</p>
        <h2>Your hormones are normal. Your brain just feels the shift more.</h2>
        <p class="lead">The difference between a hard PMS week and an easy one isn't your hormone levels. It's how strongly your brain responds to the same normal rise and fall. Two in three women feel it as mood swings.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid three">
        <article class="glass card tilt"><h3>Same hormones, different response.</h3><p>When researchers measured them, women who feel awful before their period had the same hormone levels as women who feel fine. The whole difference is sensitivity.</p><span class="cite">NIMH · Schmidt &amp; Rubinow; Hantsoo &amp; Payne, 2020</span></article>
        <article class="glass card tilt"><h3>It's wired in, and it runs in families.</h3><p>Premenstrual sensitivity is about 56 percent heritable. The same shift other people barely notice, your system actually feels. A bit like having sensitive skin.</p><span class="cite">Dubey et al, Molecular Psychiatry, 2017</span></article>
        <article class="glass card tilt"><h3>It has an end date.</h3><p>When researchers switched these hormones off, the symptoms cleared. When they switched them back on, they returned. It rolls in, and it rolls out, every cycle.</p><span class="cite">NIMH GnRH add-back studies</span></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="278" data-sat="55%">
      <div class="head center">
        <p class="eyebrow">Moon AI · during PMS</p>
        <h2>Reflect. Regulate. Respond.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid three">
        <article class="glass card big tilt">
          <div class="orb-mini orb-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="tag">Reflect</p>
          <h3>See it more than one way.</h3>
          <p>Tell Moon what happened. When you're upset, your mind locks onto one story. Moon shows you a few other ways to see it, so that one stops feeling like the truth.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="glass card big tilt">
          <div class="orb-mini orb-breathe" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <p class="tag">Regulate</p>
          <h3>Get through the twenty minutes.</h3>
          <p>A big wave of feeling takes about twenty minutes to pass. Moon gives you one small thing to do with your body to get through it, so it doesn't take over.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="glass card big tilt">
          <div class="orb-mini orb-rings" aria-hidden="true"><span class="ring r1"></span><span class="ring r2"></span><span class="ring r3"></span></div>
          <p class="tag">Respond</p>
          <h3>Send the one you won't regret.</h3>
          <p>Worked up, it's easy to say something you'll wish you hadn't. Moon writes a few ways you could reply, so you pick the one you'll feel good about, and actually send it.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="258" data-sat="58%">
      <div class="head center">
        <p class="eyebrow">Training · before PMS</p>
        <h2>Build the skill before you need it.</h2>
        <p class="lead">It's easier to stay steady when you've practised it calm. Short, playful lessons show you how to handle different feelings, so the skill is ready when you need it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid four">
        <article class="glass card tilt"><p class="tag">At work</p><h3>Handle the sharp email.</h3><p>Learn to meet a hard meeting or a pointed message without it costing you the whole day.</p></article>
        <article class="glass card tilt"><p class="tag">Between people</p><h3>Keep a small thing small.</h3><p>Read a moment before you react, so a passing friction doesn't grow into something it wasn't.</p></article>
        <article class="glass card tilt"><p class="tag">With your partner</p><h3>Name it without a fight.</h3><p>Practise telling the difference between PMS and a real issue, and bringing it up so it lands well.</p></article>
        <article class="glass card tilt"><p class="tag">Real stories</p><h3>Learn from how others handled it.</h3><p>Work through real PMS moments and the way each was handled, so the lesson sticks better than any rule.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="320" data-sat="58%">
      <div class="head center">
        <p class="eyebrow">Couples</p>
        <h2>Is it PMS, or is it real? Either way, Niyora helps.</h2>
        <p class="lead">The week before your period, your reserves run thin and small things land sharp. It isn't that you love anyone less. When you steady yourself first, there's less to spill onto the people you care about.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid three">
        <article class="glass card tilt"><p class="tag">PMS or real?</p><h3>Know which one you're in.</h3><p>A quick read on whether the feeling is the week talking or a real thing to raise. Both are valid. Knowing which changes what you do next.</p></article>
        <article class="glass card tilt"><p class="tag">Say it well</p><h3>A message, already written.</h3><p>Tips and ready-to-send lines for the hard conversations, so a plain ask is easier to meet than a mood to read.</p></article>
        <article class="glass card tilt"><p class="tag">After a fight</p><h3>Come back from it.</h3><p>If it blew up, Niyora hands you a short, honest message to reopen it. One rough moment isn't the whole story.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="230" data-sat="60%">
      <div class="head center">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why not just use ChatGPT</p>
        <h2>A frontier model keeps you talking. Moon helps you need it less.</h2>
        <p class="lead">General AI is built to hold your attention. That is the opposite of what a hard PMS moment needs. Here is the difference, line by line.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="compare">
        <div class="c them">
          <p class="c-h">Any frontier model</p>
          <p>Built to keep the conversation going. It optimizes for time spent.</p>
          <p>Agrees with you. That is what keeps you talking.</p>
          <p>Lets you vent for as long as you like. Research says venting often makes it worse.</p>
          <p>Gives endless options and keeps going.</p>
          <p>Learns a lot about you, and is built to sound like a friend. That builds dependence.</p>
          <p>Doesn't know your PMS, and rarely raises how your actions land on others.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="c us">
          <p class="c-h">Moon in Niyora</p>
          <p>Built to finish the loop, then stop. It optimizes for you needing it less.</p>
          <p>Shows you the other side on purpose. On your side, even when that means slowing you down.</p>
          <p>Helps you regulate first, so you respond with something you won't regret.</p>
          <p>Gets you to one response you can stand behind, then stops.</p>
          <p>No sign in, so you are never identifiable. It never calls itself human.</p>
          <p>Built for your PMS week, and keeps the people around you in view.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="lead center close">No ads, no profile, nothing sold. There is no version of Niyora that makes money from your worst moment.</p>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="248" data-sat="62%">
      <div class="head center">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research backed</p>
        <h2>Over 30 science-backed activities. Every one has a paper behind it.</h2>
        <p class="lead">No mystic wellness talk. Just practices drawn from peer-reviewed research, cited so you can read the source yourself. Niyora also recognises how strong your PMS is with a short test, and points to the lifestyle changes that actually move the needle.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid four dense">
        <article class="glass paper"><b>Differential hormone sensitivity</b><span>Schmidt et al, NEJM. PMDD brains react to normal hormone levels.</span></article>
        <article class="glass paper"><b>The heritable trait</b><span>Dubey et al, 2017. Sensitivity is partly in your genes.</span></article>
        <article class="glass paper"><b>GABA and the calm brake</b><span>Allopregnanolone shifts your built-in calm before your period.</span></article>
        <article class="glass paper"><b>Progressive muscle relaxation</b><span>RCT. A large effect on premenstrual symptoms.</span></article>
        <article class="glass paper"><b>Calcium for PMS</b><span>Thys-Jacobs crossover RCT. One of the strongest nutrient findings.</span></article>
        <article class="glass paper"><b>Box Breathing</b><span>Used in Navy SEAL training. Lowers cortisol, improves HRV.</span></article>
        <article class="glass paper"><b>4-7-8 Breath</b><span>Activates the parasympathetic nervous system. Weil, A.</span></article>
        <article class="glass paper"><b>5-4-3-2-1 Grounding</b><span>Linehan, 1993 (DBT). Reduces panic and dissociation.</span></article>
      </div>
      <p class="fine center">and more, every card in Niyora traces back to a source.</p>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="210" data-sat="60%">
      <div class="head center">
        <p class="eyebrow">Private by design</p>
        <h2>Built to know almost nothing about you.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Your cycle and your feelings are the most personal data there is. Niyora is built so almost none of it reaches anyone, including the AI. Moon uses AI to write its reflections, so we're plain about exactly what it can and can't see.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid three">
        <article class="glass card tilt"><div class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</div><h3>No sign in</h3><p>No account, no login. Nothing you write is ever tied to your name.</p></article>
        <article class="glass card tilt"><div class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</div><h3>Your details never reach the AI</h3><p>Before your words go to Moon's AI, names and identifying details are stripped on your phone. What is left can't point back to you.</p></article>
        <article class="glass card tilt"><div class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</div><h3>Nothing sold, nothing kept</h3><p>No ads, no profile, no data sold. Your period dates stay on your device, and are never shared.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="335" data-sat="60%">
      <div class="glass slab founder">
        <img src="/neha.jpg" alt="Neha Prasad" loading="lazy" />
        <p class="eyebrow">Why I built Niyora</p>
        <p class="quote">I went looking for a way through PMS that didn't ask me to change my body.</p>
        <p>I'm a doctor, so I started where I trust: the research. Most of what's offered for PMS either medicates it or just tracks it. Very little helps you in the actual hard hour.</p>
        <p>Then I found the quieter, stronger thread. The most reliable, least invasive way through a hard PMS week is emotion regulation. No hormones to take, no device to wear, no data to hand over.</p>
        <p>Everything in the app is one small rep of emotion regulation, done in about a minute. I built it for myself first. Now it's yours.</p>
        <p class="sig">Neha Prasad. Doctor, builder, founder of Niyora.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section data-hue="30" data-sat="70%">
      <div class="glass slab center final">
        <h2>Want Niyora when you need it?</h2>
        <p class="lead">Tap to say you're interested. No email, no account, nothing to sign. Just a nudge that tells us to keep building.</p>
        <button type="button" class="btn">I'm interested</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="back"><a href="/lab/">← back to the lab</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Tactile: heavier glass, thicker blur, deeper shadow, bigger radius, and
     a moving sheen. Cards lift and tilt toward the pointer on hover. All CSS. */
  .tc { position: relative; z-index: 2; max-width: 1160px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 clamp(18px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .tc section { padding: clamp(70px, 12vh, 130px) 0; }

  .eyebrow { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 55%, 78%, 0.8); margin-bottom: 16px; transition: color 1.4s ease; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(38px, 6.2vw, 68px); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.97); margin-bottom: 22px; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  h3 { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94); margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.35; }
  p { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.66); }
  .lead { font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 20px); color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); }
  .center { text-align: center; }
  .head { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto 44px; }
  .head.center h2, .head.center .lead { margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .head.center .lead { max-width: 60ch; }

  /* The material. Bolder than production: more blur, brighter rim light,
     a diagonal sheen layer that sweeps on hover. */
  .glass {
    position: relative;
    border-radius: 28px;
    background:
      linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.09), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 40%),
      rgba(34, 27, 54, 0.58);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16);
    box-shadow:
      0 30px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5),
      0 2px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08) inset,
      0 -20px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25) inset;
    backdrop-filter: blur(30px) saturate(1.5);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(30px) saturate(1.5);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .glass::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(115deg, transparent 30%, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14) 48%, transparent 62%);
    transform: translateX(-120%);
    transition: transform 0.9s ease;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .glass:hover::after { transform: translateX(120%); }

  .hero-card, .slab { padding: clamp(36px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .tc-hero { min-height: 92vh; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  .hero-card { text-align: center; max-width: 720px; }
  .brand { font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 5px; text-transform: uppercase; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45); margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .subhead { font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 21px); color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72); max-width: 46ch; margin: 0 auto 34px; }
  .trust { font-size: 14px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.52); margin-top: 12px; }
  .trust.strong { color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 82%, 0.95); font-weight: 500; transition: color 1.4s ease; }

  .slab.center { text-align: center; max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; }

  /* Grids of chunky, liftable cards. */
  .grid { display: grid; gap: 20px; }
  .grid.three { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); }
  .grid.four { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); }
  .grid.four.dense { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }

  .card { padding: 30px 28px; }
  .card.big { padding: 36px 30px; }
  .card .cite { display: block; margin-top: 14px; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.4px; color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 55%, 76%, 0.85); transition: color 1.4s ease; }
  .card p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.68); }
  .tag { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 78%, 0.85); margin-bottom: 12px; transition: color 1.4s ease; }

  /* Pronounced but calm motion: lift, gentle skew toward viewer, brighter rim. */
  .tilt { transition: transform 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), box-shadow 0.4s ease, border-color 0.4s ease; will-change: transform; }
  .tilt:hover {
    transform: translateY(-8px) perspective(900px) rotateX(3deg) scale(1.015);
    border-color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 68%, 0.45);
    box-shadow:
      0 44px 100px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55),
      0 0 0 1px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 70%, 0.25),
      0 2px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12) inset;
  }

  .check { width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 15px; margin-bottom: 14px; background: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 50%, 50%, 0.22); border: 1px solid hsla(var(--orb-hue), 50%, 60%, 0.5); color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 70%, 85%, 1); transition: all 1.4s ease; }

  .compare { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 18px; max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .c { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; padding: 26px; border-radius: 22px; }
  .c.them { background: rgba(20, 18, 26, 0.42); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); }
  .c.them p { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5); }
  .c.us { background: rgba(34, 27, 54, 0.58); border: 1px solid hsla(var(--orb-hue), 55%, 60%, 0.38); box-shadow: 0 20px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4); }
  .c.us p { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); }
  .c p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .c-h { font-size: 11px !important; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .c.them .c-h { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4) !important; }
  .c.us .c-h { color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 80%, 0.95) !important; transition: color 1.4s ease; }
  .close { margin: 40px auto 0; max-width: 640px; }

  .paper { padding: 20px 20px; }
  .paper b { display: block; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .paper span { font-size: 12px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5); line-height: 1.45; }
  .fine { font-size: 13px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.42); margin-top: 24px; }

  .founder { text-align: center; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .founder img { width: 118px; height: 118px; border-radius: 50%; object-fit: cover; margin: 0 auto 24px; display: block; border: 2px solid hsla(var(--orb-hue), 50%, 70%, 0.35); box-shadow: 0 0 30px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 55%, 0.3); transition: border-color 1.4s ease, box-shadow 1.4s ease; }
  .founder .quote { font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.35; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94); margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .founder p { margin: 0 auto 14px; max-width: 54ch; }
  .sig { font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45) !important; margin-top: 16px; }

  .final { max-width: 640px; }
  .final h2 { margin-bottom: 18px; }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block; margin-top: 8px; padding: 17px 44px; border-radius: 32px;
    font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95); cursor: pointer;
    border: 1.5px solid transparent;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(rgba(18, 13, 26, 0.92), rgba(18, 13, 26, 0.92)),
      linear-gradient(95deg, #e6a3c4, #9c5c86, #7846b0);
    background-origin: border-box; background-clip: padding-box, border-box;
    box-shadow: 0 0 40px rgba(217, 146, 176, 0.32);
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;
  }
  .btn:hover { transform: translateY(-2px) scale(1.02); box-shadow: 0 0 56px rgba(217, 146, 176, 0.5); }

  /* Mini-orbs, reused from production so the cards carry the brand motion. */
  .orb-mini { width: 60px; height: 60px; border-radius: 50%; margin-bottom: 22px; position: relative; background: radial-gradient(circle at 28% 24%, rgba(255,255,255,0.55) 0%, transparent 36%), radial-gradient(circle at 35% 30%, #ffffff 0%, hsl(220,25%,92%) 42%, hsl(220,38%,78%) 92%, hsl(220,42%,74%) 100%); box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(217,146,176,0.5), 0 0 38px rgba(156,92,134,0.28); }
  @keyframes orbHeartbeat { 0%,30%,60%,100% { transform: scale(1); } 8% { transform: scale(1.12); } 14% { transform: scale(1.04); } 20% { transform: scale(1.1); } 72% { transform: scale(1.06); } 80% { transform: scale(1.02); } }
  .orb-pulse { animation: orbHeartbeat 3.4s ease-in-out infinite; }
  @keyframes orbBreathe2 { 0%,100% { transform: scale(0.9); box-shadow: 0 0 12px hsla(var(--orb-hue),60%,50%,0.3); } 50% { transform: scale(1.18); box-shadow: 0 0 32px hsla(var(--orb-hue),70%,65%,0.7); } }
  .orb-breathe { animation: orbBreathe2 8s ease-in-out infinite; }
  .orb-rings { overflow: visible; }
  .orb-rings .ring { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid hsla(var(--orb-hue),60%,70%,0.55); transform: translate(-50%,-50%); opacity: 0; transition: border-color 1.4s ease; }
  .orb-rings .r1 { width: 84px; height: 84px; animation: ringFade 4.5s ease-in-out 0s infinite; }
  .orb-rings .r2 { width: 114px; height: 114px; animation: ringFade 4.5s ease-in-out 0.6s infinite; }
  .orb-rings .r3 { width: 144px; height: 144px; animation: ringFade 4.5s ease-in-out 1.2s infinite; }
  @keyframes ringFade { 0% { opacity: 0; transform: translate(-50%,-50%) scale(0.85); } 35% { opacity: 0.7; } 70% { opacity: 0.4; transform: translate(-50%,-50%) scale(1); } 100% { opacity: 0; transform: translate(-50%,-50%) scale(1.05); } }

  .back { text-align: center; padding: 50px 0 100px; }
  .back a { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5); text-decoration: none; }
  .back a:hover { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .compare { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .glass::after { display: none; }
    .tilt:hover { transform: translateY(-4px); }
    .orb-pulse, .orb-breathe { animation: none; }
    .orb-rings .ring { display: none; }
  }

  .lab-label {
    position: fixed; left: 16px; bottom: 16px; z-index: 50;
    padding: 8px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.5px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
    background: rgba(34, 27, 54, 0.6); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18);
    backdrop-filter: blur(16px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px);
  }
</style>
